      "gloss": "punctuation, the marking of divisions between words",
      "evidence": [
        "Cic. Mur. 25: <span lang=\"la\">interpūnctiōnēs verbōrum</span> (Lewis &amp; Short)",
        "Traupman 248, 367"
      ],
      "comment": "The verb is <span lang=\"la\">interpungere</span>, to punctuate: <span lang=\"la\">cum scrībimus, interpungere cōnsuēvimus</span>, when we write we are used to punctuating (Sen. Ep. 40, Lewis &amp; Short). A punctuation mark is <span lang=\"la\">interpūnctum</span> (Cic. de Or. 3.181; Traupman 248). Ancient Latin marked word divisions with points; the modern marks have modern names (see comma, full stop, question mark)."
